<title>UK: Algeria sees 1997 oil exports rise slowing up - OPEC.</title>
<headline>Algeria sees 1997 oil exports rise slowing up - OPEC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria expects its oil exports to rise by 8.2 percent this year against a 17 percent increase last year, the OPEC news agency OPECNA said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Output should increase by 6.8 percent against 6.0 percent rise last year, OPECNA said, quoting Algerian minister of energy and mines Amar Makhloufi from an interview for Arab Oil and Gas magazine to be published on Friday.</p>
<p>Algeria's 1997 production capacity will be between 850,000 and 900,000 barrels per day (bpd) against 700,000 bpd &quot;not long ago&quot;, Makhloufi said.</p>
<p>Natural gas exports should rise by more than 25 percent this year to 52 billion cubic metres against a 9.5 percent increase in 1996, he said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7629</p>
